      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "(b)",
      "bbox": [
        400.614013671875,
        286.20458984375,
        409.90704345703125,
        289.81500244140625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fig. 4",
      "bbox": [
        102.96600341796875,
        307.68951416015625,
        126.76766204833984,
        316.5864562988281
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "DCA’s ECDFs for instance A. Fig. 4(b) is a zoom of Fig. 4(a) for DCAs up to 500 meters.",
      "bbox": [
        136.7306671142578,
        307.68951416015625,
        509.04827880859375,
        316.5864562988281
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "It is important to underline that the lower and upper distributions do not necessarily result in lower and upper bounds",
      "bbox": [
        86.94400024414062,
        343.5157470703125,
        540.0206909179688,
        348.02899169921875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "for the collision probability at values of the threshold δDCA̸ = 50m. Speciﬁcally, the lower and upper distributions are",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        361.0436706542969,
        540.0089721679688,
        371.38482666015625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "not lower and upper envelopes for the ECDFs resulting from the imprecise set, but they are distributions belonging to",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        383.3737487792969,
        540.0169067382812,
        387.8869934082031
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "the set itself bounding the expectation of a speciﬁc quantity of interest. From Fig. 4 we can see that the lower and upper",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        403.3037414550781,
        540.1910400390625,
        407.8169860839844
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "distributions that bound the PoC for δDCA = 50m are not bounding the ECDFs for thresholds larger than ≈100 m.",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        420.27374267578125,
        541.7435913085938,
        431.1728210449219
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Even more, from Fig. 4(a) we can see that the green line is above the red one for DCA thresholds larger than ≈20 km.",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        440.2027282714844,
        541.7037963867188,
        449.6078186035156
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The ellipses and ECDFs are reconstructed from the uncertainty propagation of the TLE-derived uncertainties. ESA’s",
      "bbox": [
        86.94400024414062,
        463.0917663574219,
        539.999267578125,
        467.6050109863281
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "guidelines for pure Two-Line Elements (TLE) screening, set a threshold of PoC > 10−4 for δDCA = 300 m to trigger",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        478.6885070800781,
        540.1661376953125,
        490.9608154296875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "further analyses. For such distance, by visual inspection of Fig. 4(b), the upper probability is PoC300m > 5 · 10−4.",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        498.6175231933594,
        541.7435913085938,
        510.8908386230469
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Thus, the upper probability value ﬂags up a potential collision that needs to be further investigated. On the other hand,",
      "bbox": [
        71.69100189208984,
        522.8797607421875,
        541.2587890625,
        527.3930053710938
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "the lower probability is PoC300m < 1 · 10−5, which would indicate a near-safe conjunction. The diﬀerence between",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        538.4764404296875,
        540.0128784179688,
        551.8698120117188
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "these two bounds is the reason why it is critical to model and handle epistemic uncertainty in collision risk assessment.",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        562.7377319335938,
        541.7632446289062,
        567.2509765625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Speciﬁcally, the width of the probability interval indicates the degree of ignorance of the probability estimate. Thus, it",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        582.6677856445312,
        540.0203857421875,
        587.1810302734375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "should be used to support the decision-maker and decide whether to acquire new measurements or to manoeuvre. In the",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        602.5967407226562,
        540.01513671875,
        607.1099853515625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "next sections, we will use the distance threshold of δDCA = 50m as it is tailored for the satellites under assessment.",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        620.1256713867188,
        531.8648681640625,
        630.466796875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "2. Collision instance",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        654.14013671875,
        155.21096801757812,
        662.9673461914062
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "For instance B, a tracking campaign with M = 12 noisy observations is considered between the satellites’ epoch",
      "bbox": [
        86.94400024414062,
        673.9296875,
        540.0093383789062,
        682.7767944335938
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "dates and 24 h before the rTCA. At this cut-oﬀtime, the RPF is run to estimate the PoC bounds. The ellipses resulting",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        693.8587036132812,
        540.0057373046875,
        702.705810546875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
